mediatek: filogic: build PCA953x GPIO + PCA954x i2c-mux into kernel (r4-pro)

r4-pro's err/act system LEDs sit on a PCA9555 GPIO expander behind a PCA9545
i2c-mux on i2c2. Build the expander + mux drivers into the kernel so the LED
chain probes early; as modules the LEDs only come up after rootfs. The 10G WAN
PHY (phy28) reset is a SoC GPIO pulsed in u-boot (z13), NOT on the PCA9555 -- an
earlier comment claiming the PHY reset hung off the expander was wrong.
diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12 b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
index 1fae94f..2aecc44 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
@@ -211,6 +211,7 @@ CONFIG_GENERIC_STRNLEN_USER=y
 CONFIG_GENERIC_TIME_VSYSCALL=y
 CONFIG_GLOB=y
 CONFIG_GPIO_CDEV=y
+CONFIG_GPIO_PCA953X=y
 CONFIG_GPIO_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_GPIO_WATCHDOG_ARCH_INITCALL=y
 CONFIG_GRO_CELLS=y
@@ -227,6 +228,7 @@ CONFIG_I2C=y
 CONFIG_I2C_BOARDINFO=y
 CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=y
 CONFIG_I2C_MT65XX=y
+CONFIG_I2C_MUX_PCA954x=y
 CONFIG_ICPLUS_PHY=y
 # CONFIG_IDPF is not set
 CONFIG_ILLEGAL_POINTER_VALUE=0xdead000000000000
